imx8mp-evk: leave the on-board eMMC (uSDHC3) to the TEE

OP-TEE drives uSDHC3 from the secure world for its RPMB storage. U-Boot
proper still probed the controller (bootstd scans every MMC device) and
left both it and the card in 8-bit HS400ES with its own clock, so the
first RPMB access after that no longer matched the state OP-TEE had set
up. The board boots from SD and never needs the eMMC in U-Boot, so keep
U-Boot off it entirely.

Upstream-Status: Inappropriate [board configuration for the TEE-owned eMMC]

--- a/arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-evk-u-boot.dtsi
+++ b/arch/arm/dts/imx8mp-evk-u-boot.dtsi
@@ -232,6 +232,8 @@
 };
 
 &usdhc3 {
+	/* Owned by OP-TEE (RPMB secure storage); never touched by U-Boot */
+	status = "disabled";
 	bootph-pre-ram;
 	mmc-hs400-1_8v;
 	mmc-hs400-enhanced-strobe;
